>
  <p>
    Short, self-contained recipes for the things you do every day with MIDI. Each one is shown in up to four
    ecosystems: the browser's <a href="/libraries/?q=web%20midi">Web MIDI API</a>, Python with
    <a href="/libraries/?q=mido">mido</a>, C++ with <a href="/libraries/?q=rtmidi">RtMidi</a>, and Rust with
    <a href="/libraries/?q=midir">midir</a> and <a href="/libraries/?q=midly">midly</a>. They open the first available
    port to stay short; real programs should let the user pick a port by name.
  </p>

