  <Callout type="note" title="Web MIDI snippets">
    <p>
      The browser examples use top-level <code>await</code>, so run them in a module script or the DevTools console.
      Web MIDI needs a secure context (HTTPS or <code>localhost</code>) and a user permission prompt. You can try them
      right now on the <a href="/try/">live monitor</a> page's console.
    </p>
  </Callout>
  <Callout type="info" title="Tested">
    <p>
      Every snippet on this page was run on macOS against a virtual MIDI port: mido 1.3.3 with python-rtmidi 1.5.8,
      @tonejs/midi 2.0.28, midi-file 1.2.4, RtMidi 6.0.0, midir 0.11.1 and midly 0.5.3. The Web MIDI snippets were
      run in Node through the <code>web-midi-api</code> polyfill. Build the C++ examples with
      <code>c++ -std=c++17 main.cpp $(pkg-config --cflags --libs rtmidi)</code>, or compile
